## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to receive and utilize the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes advertised by EBGP peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to receive and utilize the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes advertised by EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv6
            send-to-ebgp ipv6
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. These commands will:
1. Enable receiving the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes from EBGP peers (`add-to-received-ebgp`)
2. Allow sending the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes to EBGP peers (`send-to-ebgp`)

If you need to apply this to a specific neighbor rather than the entire group, use:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            link-bandwidth
                add-to-received-ebgp ipv6
                send-to-ebgp ipv6
```
