To configure a Nokia router's BGP group to receive and utilize the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes advertised by EBGP peers, use these CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv6
            send-to-ebgp ipv6
```

If you want to automatically add link-bandwidth to received EBGP routes:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv6
```

For aggregating bandwidth values from multipaths:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            aggregate-used-paths ipv6
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. These commands enable the router to accept, process, and propagate the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv6 routes with EBGP peers.
