To disable the capability of sending/receiving multiple paths per prefix in BGP on a Nokia router, you need to ensure that multipath and ECMP features are not enabled. Since the reference content doesn't explicitly provide a direct command for disabling multipath, the closest relevant configuration would be to disable `ebgp-ibgp-equal` in the BGP best-path-selection context, which affects multipath behavior:

```
configure router
    bgp
        best-path-selection
            no ebgp-ibgp-equal
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This ensures that BGP won't treat EBGP and IBGP paths equally when considering multiple paths for the same prefix.
