## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to automatically attach link-bandwidth extended communities to all received unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes from directly connected EBGP peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to automatically attach link-bandwidth extended communities to all received unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes from directly connected EBGP peers, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure
    router
        bgp
            group <group-name>
                family ipv6
                neighbor <peer-ipv6-address>
                    export <policy-name>
                    peer-as <as-number>
            exit
            policy-options
                begin
                policy-statement <policy-name>
                    entry 10
                        from
                            protocol bgp
                            family ipv6
                        to
                            level external
                        action accept
                            community add link-bandwidth-community
                        exit
                    exit
                commit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<peer-ipv6-address>`, `<as-number>`, and `<policy-name>` with your specific values. The `link-bandwidth-community` should be predefined according to your bandwidth values.

Note that while the exact `link-bandwidth` community attachment isn't explicitly shown in the provided reference content, this configuration follows standard BGP policy structure for Nokia routers to match IPv6 EBGP routes and apply communities. You would need to define the specific link-bandwidth community values separately in your policy options.
