To configure Nokia routers to allow BGP to propagate routes that are not the best path in the routing table, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ebgp-ibgp-equal
        deterministic-med
        always-compare-med zero
    exit
exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable EIBGP equality (`ebgp-ibgp-equal`) to treat EBGP and IBGP routes equally in best path selection
2. Configure deterministic MED comparison (`deterministic-med`)
3. Always compare MED values (`always-compare-med zero`), including when routes come from different ASes

The combination of these settings modifies the BGP best path selection process to consider more routes as potential candidates for propagation.
