Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure BGP for advertising VPN IPv4 routes over IPv6 transport with an IPv6 next-hop address:

```cli
configure router bgp
    # Enable extended next-hop encoding capability for VPN-IPv4
    extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4
    
    # Configure BGP to advertise VPN-IPv4 routes with IPv6 next-hops over IPv6 transport
    advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4
    
    # Optionally enable rapid updates for VPN-IPv4 routes
    rapid-update vpn-ipv4
    
    # Configure BGP group or neighbor specific settings
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4
        neighbor <ipv6-neighbor-address>
            peer-as <as-number>
exit
```

Key points:
- `extended-nh-encoding vpn-ipv4` enables the capability to handle IPv6 next-hops for VPN-IPv4 routes
- `advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4` actually enables the advertisement with IPv6 next-hops
- The BGP peer must be configured using IPv6 addressing
- The VPN-IPv4 address family must be enabled in the BGP group or neighbor configuration
