## User question:
"How to configure a Nokia router to allow advertising active /32 LDP FEC prefixes to a BGP peer with an RFC 3107 label, regardless of existing BGP paths for the same prefix?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise active /32 LDP FEC prefixes to a BGP peer with RFC 3107 labels (regardless of existing BGP paths), use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family label-ipv4
        neighbor <peer-ip-address>
            family label-ipv4
            extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
exit
```

Key points:
- The `family label-ipv4` enables BGP to carry labeled IPv4 prefixes (RFC 3107)
- The `extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4` ensures proper next-hop encoding for labeled routes

This configuration will allow the router to advertise all active LDP /32 FECs to the specified BGP peer with their associated labels, independent of other BGP paths for the same prefixes.
