To configure a Nokia router to advertise active /32 LDP FEC prefixes to a BGP peer with an RFC 3107 label, regardless of existing BGP paths for the same prefix, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv4
    exit
exit
```

This configuration ensures that the BGP decision process treats EBGP and IBGP routes equally for labeled IPv4 prefixes (/32 LDP FEC), allowing them to be advertised with RFC 3107 labels even if other BGP paths exist for the same prefix.
