To configure Nokia routers to allow LLGR (Long-Lived Graceful Restart) stale routes to be advertised to all peers and enable them to exit AS 65530, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        enable-notification
    exit
    group "your-group-name"
        next-hop-self
        enforce-first-as
    exit
exit
```

Key points:
- `enable-notification` under graceful-restart ensures peers are notified about route changes
- `next-hop-self` ensures proper advertisement of routes
- `enforce-first-as` maintains AS path integrity

Note: Replace "your-group-name" with your actual BGP group name. The exact implementation may require additional context about your specific topology and requirements.
