To configure a Nokia router to advertise a long-lived stale time of 3600 seconds in BGP graceful restart LLGR capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp graceful-restart
    restart-time 3600
exit
```

This command sets the BGP graceful restart time to 3600 seconds at the global BGP level. The configuration can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if needed by navigating to the respective context (`config>router>bgp>group>graceful-restart` or `config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>graceful-restart`) before entering the `restart-time 3600` command.
