## User question:
How to configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
        exit
        next-hop-self
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration will:
1. Accept link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
2. Send link-bandwidth extended communities to EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
3. Add link-bandwidth extended communities to received EBGP routes for IPv4
4. Enable next-hop-self for the group to ensure proper readvertisement
