To configure BGP on a Nokia router to aggregate bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes when readvertising with next-hop-self, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            accept-from-ebgp ipv4
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
        exit
        next-hop-self
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name. This configuration:
1. Enables acceptance of link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
2. Allows sending link-bandwidth extended communities to EBGP peers for IPv4 routes
3. Configures next-hop-self for route advertisements

The router will now preserve and aggregate the link-bandwidth values when readvertising IPv4 routes with next-hop-self.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
