To enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes spanning multiple ASes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        aigp
exit
```

This enables the Accumulated IGP (AIGP) path attribute support for the specified BGP group, allowing BGP path selection to consider end-to-end IGP metrics across multiple ASes.

If you also want to disable the consideration of next-hop metrics in the BGP decision process (which might interfere with pure IGP metric-based selection), you can additionally configure:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ignore-nh-metric
    exit
exit
```
