To enable BGP path selection based on end-to-end IGP metrics for routes spanning multiple ASes on a Nokia router, you need to configure the AIGP (Accumulated IGP) attribute. Here are the required CLI commands:

1. Enter the BGP configuration context:
```
configure router bgp
```

2. Enable AIGP at either the group or neighbor level (choose one approach):

For a BGP group:
```
group <group-name>
    aigp
exit
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
group <group-name>
    neighbor <ip-address>
        aigp
    exit
exit
```

3. Optionally, you may want to disable next-hop metric consideration in the BGP best path selection if needed:
```
best-path-selection
    ignore-nh-metric
exit
```

These commands will enable BGP to use end-to-end IGP metrics for path selection across multiple ASes through the AIGP attribute.
