## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to permit BGP next-hop resolution for labeled IPv4/IPv6 and VPN-IPv4/IPv6 routes using static routes (excluding default static routes), use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp next-hop-res 
    no use-bgp-routes
exit

configure router bgp next-hop-res labeled-routes 
    transport-tunnel
exit

configure router bgp 
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4
    enforce-first-as
exit

configure router bgp best-path-selection 
    ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv4 label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
exit
```

These commands:
1. Disable recursive next-hop resolution via BGP routes (forces static route usage)
2. Enable tunnel-based next-hop resolution for labeled routes
3. Advertise extended next-hop encoding capabilities for labeled IPv4 and VPN-IPv4 routes
4. Enforce first AS validation for EBGP sessions
5. Configure equal treatment of EBGP/IBGP routes for the specified address families
