To configure a Nokia router to permit BGP next-hop resolution for labeled IPv4/IPv6 and VPN-IPv4/IPv6 routes using static routes (excluding default static routes), use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                static
                    include-ldp-over-rsvp
                    no include-default
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BGP configuration context
2. Configures next-hop resolution specifically for labeled routes
3. Enables static routes for next-hop resolution under transport-tunnel
4. Includes LDP-over-RSVP tunnels (optional, can be removed if not needed)
5. Explicitly excludes default static routes

For labeled IPv4/IPv6 and VPN-IPv4/IPv6 routes, this ensures BGP will use non-default static routes for next-hop resolution while maintaining support for other transport tunnel types if configured.
