---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a TCP authentication keychain named "secure_bgp123" for BGP sessions on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp auth-keychain secure_bgp123
```

This command should be executed under the BGP configuration context (`config>router>bgp`). The keychain can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if needed.
---
