Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To tie BGP neighbor session state with BFD session status on Nokia routers, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            bfd-enable
```

This command enables BFD for the specific BGP neighbor, causing the BGP session state to follow the BFD session status. The BFD parameters themselves would need to be configured separately under the relevant IP interface configuration.
