To enable BGP routing protocol on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```bash
configure router
    bgp
        router-id <ip-address>
        enforce-first-as
        rapid-withdrawal
        exit
```

Replace `<ip-address>` with your router's IPv4 address (e.g., 192.0.2.1). 

To configure BGP peers, you would additionally need to create groups and neighbors with their respective AS numbers, for example:

```bash
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            peer-as <as-number>
            neighbor <ip-address>
                peer-as <as-number>
                exit
            exit
        exit
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<as-number>`, and `<ip-address>` with your specific values.
