To configure BGP peers, you would additionally need to create groups and neighbors with their respective AS numbers, for example:

```bash
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            peer-as <as-number>
            neighbor <ip-address>
                peer-as <as-number>
                exit
            exit
        exit
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<as-number>`, and `<ip-address>` with your specific values.
