To enable BGP tunneling for next-hop resolution of labeled IPv4 routes on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    family ipv4
                        resolution-filter bgp
                        resolution-filter sr-te
                        resolution-filter sr-isis
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables BGP tunneling for next-hop resolution under the `labeled-routes` context
2. Specifies IPv4 family for the labeled routes
3. Adds BGP, SR-TE, and SR-ISIS as resolution filters for next-hop resolution

For completeness, you may also want to enable extended next-hop encoding for label-IPv4 routes if needed:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
        exit
    exit
```
