Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure BGP Monitoring Protocol (BMP) on a Nokia router:

```
configure
    bmp
        station "BMP_STATION_1" create
            report-local-routes
            connection
                station-address 192.0.2.10 port 5000
                connect-retry 300
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BMP configuration context
2. Creates a BMP monitoring station named "BMP_STATION_1"
3. Enables reporting of local routes to the BMP station
4. Configures the station address (192.0.2.10) and TCP port (5000)
5. Sets the connect retry timer to 300 seconds (5 minutes)

Adjust the station name, IP address, port number, and connect-retry timer values as needed for your specific deployment.
