undo peer <group-name> next-hop-local
查询的def
The peer next-hop-local command configures an BGP MVPNv6 device to set its IP address as the next hop of routes when the BGP-IPv6 MVPN device advertises the routes to an IBGP peer group.
The undo peer next-hop-local command restores the default setting.
By default, an BGP MVPNv6 device sets its IP address as the next hop address of routes when advertising them to its EBGP peer; the BGP device does not change the next hop address of routes when advertising them to its IBGP peer group.
