## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to prefer BGP routes with valid RPKI origin validation states over those with not-found or invalid states during best path selection?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to prefer BGP routes with valid RPKI origin validation states over those with not-found or invalid states, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        origin-invalid-unusable
        compare-origin-validation-state
    exit
exit
```

These commands will:
1. Mark routes with invalid RPKI origins as unusable (`origin-invalid-unusable`)
2. Enable comparison of origin validation states during best path selection (`compare-origin-validation-state`), which prefers valid > not-found > invalid routes
