## User question:
How to disable BGP route damping for learned routes in Nokia routers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To disable BGP route damping for learned routes in Nokia routers, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp no damp-peer-oscillations
```

This command will remove any existing BGP route damping configuration at the global BGP level. If you need to disable it specifically for a group or neighbor, navigate to the respective context first:

For a BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> no damp-peer-oscillations
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> no damp-peer-oscillations
```
