To configure a Nokia router's BGP group to treat received EVPN routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default, you need to create a route policy that matches EVPN routes lacking the encapsulation extended community and applies the VXLAN encapsulation. Then apply this policy as an import policy to the BGP group.

Here are the CLI commands:

```
# Create a route policy to match EVPN routes without encapsulation and set VXLAN
configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement EVPN-VXLAN-DEFAULT
    entry 10
        from protocol bgp-evpn
        from community missing-encap
        action accept
            encapsulation-type vxlan
        exit
    exit
commit
exit

# Apply the policy to the BGP group
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    import EVPN-VXLAN-DEFAULT
exit
```

Note: The exact implementation might require additional details about how to match routes missing the encapsulation extended community (represented here by the placeholder `missing-encap` community). You would need to define this community matching condition appropriately in your policy based on your specific requirements.
