To configure a Nokia router's BGP group to treat received EVPN routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> vpn-apply-import
```

This command applies the base instance BGP import route policies to EVPN routes, which includes handling routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia router's BGP group to treat received EVPN routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router's BGP group to treat received EVPN routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> vpn-apply-import
```

This command applies the base instance BGP import route policies to EVPN routes, which includes handling routes without encapsulation extended community as VXLAN by default.
---
