To configure a Nokia router to advertise the default BGP route (0.0.0.0/0) to specific peers within an established BGP group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <peer-IP> advertise-inactive
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group and `<peer-IP>` with the IP address of the specific peer(s) you want to advertise the default route to. 

