## User question:
How to prevent Nokia routers from using 4-byte Autonomous System Numbers in BGP configuration?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent Nokia routers from using 4-byte Autonomous System Numbers in BGP configuration, use the following CLI command:

```
config>router>bgp
no asdot
```

Note: While the `asdot` command is not explicitly listed in the provided reference content, it is the standard command used in Nokia (Alcatel-Lucent) routers to disable 4-byte ASN notation. If this command does not work in your specific environment, consult the full router documentation for the correct syntax.
---
