To configure a Nokia router to strictly support only IPv4 routing exchanges with BGP peer 192.0.2.1 without negotiating any new capabilities, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    no extended-nh-encoding
    no add-paths
    no link-state-import-enable
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            no enable-notification
            no advertise-inactive
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name. This configuration:
- Disables extended next-hop encoding capabilities
- Disables add-paths functionality
- Disables link-state information import
- Explicitly disables notification capability for graceful restart
- Prevents advertising inactive routes

The configuration ensures only basic IPv4 routing exchanges occur with the specified BGP peer.
