## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to prevent BGP peers from negotiating new capabilities while maintaining strict IPv4 routing exchange support?
---
## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP peers from negotiating new capabilities while maintaining strict IPv4 routing exchange support, use the following CLI commands:

```
config>router>bgp>group
    disable-capability-negotiation
```

Or for a specific neighbor within a group:
```
config>router>bgp>group>neighbor
    disable-capability-negotiation
```

These commands will disable capability negotiation with BGP peers while ensuring IPv4 routing exchanges continue to function strictly.
