To configure a Nokia router to remove standard and large BGP communities when advertising routes to a specific peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group "PEER_GROUP_NAME"
        neighbor "PEER_IP_ADDRESS"
            no send-communities
```

Replace `"PEER_GROUP_NAME"` with your BGP peer group name and `"PEER_IP_ADDRESS"` with the IP address of the specific peer. The `no send-communities` command ensures that both standard and large BGP communities are removed when advertising routes to this peer.
