To prevent BGP sessions from using fast external failover on a Nokia router, you need to adjust the BGP timers. Specifically, you should modify the keepalive timer to increase the interval between keepalive messages. Here are the CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        keepalive 60
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This increases the keepalive timer from the default 30 seconds to 60 seconds, which will slow down the detection of session failures compared to the default setting.

For neighbor-specific configurations:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            keepalive 60
        exit
    exit
exit
```

These commands will make the BGP session less aggressive in detecting failures by sending keepalive messages less frequently.
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
