To prevent all IPv4 and IPv6 BGP routes from being installed into RTM and FIB on a Nokia router, use the following CLI configuration commands:

```
configure router bgp
    no rapid-update label-ipv4 label-ipv6 vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
exit
```

These commands disable BGP rapid update for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled and VPN routes, effectively preventing them from being installed into the routing table manager (RTM) and forwarding information base (FIB).
