To prevent Nokia routers from installing both labeled and unlabeled BGP routes into RTM and FIB while maintaining the BGP session, you can use route policies with the `import` command to filter out unwanted routes. Here's the configuration:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement FILTER-BGP-ROUTES
            entry 10
                from
                    protocol bgp
                action reject
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        group "BGP-GROUP"
            neighbor "NEIGHBOR-IP"
                import "FILTER-BGP-ROUTES"
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Creates a policy named "FILTER-BGP-ROUTES" that rejects all BGP routes
2. Applies this policy to inbound routes from the specified BGP neighbor using the `import` command

The BGP session will remain established, but no routes will be installed in RTM/FIB. Adjust the neighbor IP/group name as needed for your specific deployment.
------------
