To configure a Nokia router to accept a maximum of 1024 dynamic BGP sessions from remote peers within a specific BGP peer group, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <peer-group-name> dynamic-neighbor-limit 1024
```

Replace `<peer-group-name>` with the name of your BGP peer group. This command sets the maximum number of dynamic BGP sessions to 1024 for the specified peer group.
