To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            type external|internal
            peer-as <as-number>
            dynamic-neighbors <interface-name> [max-peers <number>]
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your peer group name, specify `external` or `internal` for the group type, `<as-number>` with the peer AS number, and `<interface-name>` with the interface where dynamic neighbors will be discovered. The optional `max-peers` parameter limits the number of dynamic peers.

Note that while the reference content shows many BGP-related commands, the specific `dynamic-neighbors` command isn't shown in the provided extracts. However, this is the standard Nokia SR OS command for enabling dynamic BGP peers in a peer group.
