To enable dynamic BGP session configuration for a peer group on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
            enable-peer-tracking
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired peer group name and `<remote-as-number>` with the autonomous system number of the remote peer. 

The `enable-peer-tracking` command is optional but recommended as it accelerates BGP re-convergence by dropping peers immediately when their route becomes unavailable.
