## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers for VPN route exchange between different autonomous systems in a BGP environment, use the following CLI commands:

```plaintext
configure router
    bgp
        # Configure router ID
        router-id <ip-address>

        # Enable third-party next-hop for EBGP peers in the same subnet
        third-party-nexthop

        # Configure leak-import policy for route exchange between routing instances
        rib-management
            ipv4
                leak-import <policy-name>
            exit
            label-ipv4
                leak-import <policy-name>
            exit
            ipv6
                leak-import <policy-name>
            exit
        exit

        # Enable next-hop-self for VPN routes
        group <group-name>
            next-hop-self
            enable-peer-tracking
            neighbor <neighbor-ip>
                peer-as <remote-as-number>
                # Optional: Configure local AS if needed
                local-as <as-number> [private] [no-prepend-global-as]
            exit
        exit

        # Enable extended next-hop encoding for VPN routes
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4

        # Configure best path selection to treat EBGP and IBGP equally
        best-path-selection
            ebgp-ibgp-equal vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
        exit

        # Configure transport tunnel for labeled routes
        next-hop-resolution
            labeled-routes
                transport-tunnel
                    # Add tunnel configuration as needed
                exit
            exit
        exit

        # Configure prefix limits for VPN routes
        group <group-name>
            prefix-limit vpn-ipv4 <limit> threshold <percentage>
            prefix-limit vpn-ipv6 <limit> threshold <percentage>
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace placeholders (`<ip-address>`, `<policy-name>`, `<group-name>`, `<neighbor-ip>`, `<remote-as-number>`, `<as-number>`, `<limit>`, `<percentage>`) with your specific values. The configuration enables VPN route exchange between autonomous systems with proper route leaking, next-hop handling, and path selection.
