To configure a Nokia router to reject EBGP routes where the last AS in the AS_PATH does not match the peer's configured AS, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp enforce-first-as
```

This command ensures that all routes received from an EBGP peer are checked to verify that the most recent ASN in the AS_PATH matches the configured `peer-as` of the session. If there is a mismatch, the route will be rejected. 

Apply this command at the global BGP level, or alternatively at the BGP group or neighbor level if you want to enforce it selectively:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> enforce-first-as
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> enforce-first-as
```
------------
As a network device expert, please determine whether the following answer correctly responds to the user's question based on the router configuration manual. Only output "Correct" or "Incorrect" without any explanation or additional information. You must make your own judgment based on the Router configuration manual provided to you, not on your own knowledge.
---
## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to reject EBGP routes where the last AS in the AS_PATH does not match the peer's configured AS?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to reject EBGP routes where the last AS in the AS_PATH does not match the peer's configured AS, use the following command:

```
configure router bgp enforce-first-as
```

This command ensures that all routes received from an EBGP peer are checked to verify that the most recent ASN in the AS_PATH matches the configured `peer-as` of the session. If there is a mismatch, the route will be rejected. 

Apply this command at the global BGP level, or alternatively at the BGP group or neighbor level if you want to enforce it selectively:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> enforce-first-as
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> enforce-first-as
```
