## User question:
How to ensure that all routes received from an EBGP peer on a Nokia router have their most recent ASN in the AS_PATH attribute matching the configured peer AS of the session?
---
## Proposed answer:
To ensure that all routes received from an EBGP peer have their most recent ASN in the AS_PATH attribute matching the configured peer AS of the session, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp enforce-first-as
```

This can also be applied at the group or neighbor level if needed:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> enforce-first-as
```

or

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> enforce-first-as
```
