To restrict BGP next-hop resolution for labeled routes to only use LSPs that have been explicitly tagged, you need to create a route policy that filters LSPs based on tags and apply it to BGP next-hop resolution. Here are the required CLI commands:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement LSP-TAG-POLICY
            entry 10
                from
                    tag <your-tag-value>
                action accept
            exit
            default-action reject
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            policy LSP-TAG-POLICY
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<your-tag-value>` with the specific tag value you want to use for identifying acceptable LSPs. This configuration ensures that only LSPs carrying the specified tag will be used for BGP next-hop resolution of labeled routes.
