To configure a Nokia router to restrict BGP next-hop resolution to only use labeled routes from tunnels explicitly marked with admin tags, use the following CLI commands:

```bash
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution labeled-routes transport-tunnel family resolution-filter
    no sr-te
    no sr-isis
    no sr-ospf3
    no bgp
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Navigates to the BGP next-hop resolution context for labeled routes
2. Disables all automatic tunnel type selections (SR-TE, SR-ISIS, SR-OSPFv3, BGP)
3. Ensures only explicitly configured/admin-tagged tunnels will be used for BGP next-hop resolution

Note: You'll need to separately configure the specific admin tags on your tunnels through the appropriate tunnel configuration contexts.
