To configure Nokia router's BGP to advertise the capability to receive VPN IPv4 routes with NLRI AFI=1, NLRI SAFI=128, and next-hop AFI=2, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        family vpn-ipv4
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables the VPN-IPv4 address family (AFI=1, SAFI=128) capability for BGP peers in the specified group. The next-hop AFI=2 (IPv6) is automatically supported when the VPN-IPv4 family is enabled, as this is part of the standard BGP VPN capability negotiation.
