## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router's BGP session to support IPv6 multicast VPN (mcast-vpn-ipv6) alongside the default IPv4 unicast, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    rapid-update mcast-vpn-ipv6
    vpn-apply-import
exit
```

For BGP groups or neighbors where you want to apply this configuration:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    family mcast-vpn-ipv6
    no disable-capability-negotiation
exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable rapid updates for mcast-vpn-ipv6 at the global BGP level
2. Apply base instance import policies to VPN routes including mcast-vpn-ipv6
3. Add the mcast-vpn-ipv6 address family to the BGP group
4. Ensure capability negotiation is enabled (default setting)

Note that you'll need to replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name.
