To configure a Nokia router to advertise IPv6 multicast routes from a VPRN over the provider network using BGP, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        rapid-update mvpn-ipv6
        vpn-apply-import
        group "PROVIDER_BGP_GROUP"
            family vpn-ipv6 mvpn-ipv6
            advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv6
            next-hop-self
            neighbor <PEER_IP_ADDRESS>
                peer-as <PEER_AS_NUMBER>
                export "EXPORT_POLICY_NAME"
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Key points:
1. Enable rapid updates for MVPN-IPv6 routes
2. Apply import policies to VPN routes
3. Configure BGP group with VPN-IPv6 and MVPN-IPv6 address families
4. Advertise IPv6 next-hops for VPN-IPv6 routes
5. Enable next-hop-self to rewrite next-hop addresses
6. Specify neighbor details and apply export policy

Make sure to replace `<PEER_IP_ADDRESS>`, `<PEER_AS_NUMBER>`, and `"EXPORT_POLICY_NAME"` with your actual values. Also ensure you have created the appropriate export policy to control which routes are advertised.
