## User question:
How to configure Nokia router for resolving next-hop of unlabeled IPv6 BGP routes using shortcut tunnels?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router for resolving next-hop of unlabeled IPv6 BGP routes using shortcut tunnels, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv6
        rapid-update label-ipv6
        extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4
exit all
```

These commands:
1. Enable equal treatment of EBGP and IBGP routes for IPv6 (`ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv6`)
2. Enable rapid update for labeled IPv6 routes (`rapid-update label-ipv6`)
3. Configure extended next-hop encoding capabilities for label-IPv4 and VPN-IPv4 routes (`extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4 vpn-ipv4`)

This configuration allows the router to properly handle next-hop resolution for unlabeled IPv6 BGP routes through shortcut tunnels while maintaining compatibility with labeled IPv4 and VPN IPv4 routes.
