To enable BGP flowspec validation on a Nokia router, you need to enter the BGP configuration context and configure origin validation for the desired address families. Here are the CLI commands:

1. Enter the BGP configuration context:
```
configure router bgp
```

2. Depending on where you want to apply the validation (group or neighbor level), navigate to the appropriate context. For example, for a group:
```
group <group-name>
enable-origin-validation ipv4 ipv6
```

Or for a specific neighbor:
```
group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
enable-origin-validation ipv4 ipv6
```

Note: You can specify individual address families (ipv4, ipv6, label-ipv4, label-ipv6) based on your requirements.
