To configure BGP on a Nokia router to maintain the session permanently while rejecting any proposed hold-time below 120 seconds, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    keepalive 40
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <neighbor-IP>
            peer-as <remote-AS-number>
            enforce-first-as
            no shutdown
exit
```

The `keepalive 40` command ensures the hold-time is set to 120 seconds (hold-time = 3 × keepalive interval), rejecting any proposed hold-time below this value. The session will remain up as long as the keepalive messages are exchanged within this interval. Adjust `<group-name>`, `<neighbor-IP>`, and `<remote-AS-number>` as needed.
