## User question:
In Nokia routers, how would you modify BGP best path selection to exclude the resolved distance metric when comparing routes with identical NLRI from base router BGP peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To modify BGP best path selection to exclude the resolved distance metric when comparing routes with identical NLRI from base router BGP peers, use the following CLI configuration:

```
configure router bgp best-path-selection deterministic-med
```

This command ensures deterministic MED comparison by grouping paths based on neighbor AS before comparing MED values, effectively removing any dependency on the order of route arrival.
