Here are the CLI configuration commands to create a BGP inbound route policy named "CustomerX_Policy" with a secondary fallback policy expression "LocalPref_100":

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement "CustomerX_Policy"
            entry 10
                action accept
                exit
            exit
        policy-statement "LocalPref_100"
            entry 10
                action accept
                    local-preference 100
                exit
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            neighbor <neighbor-ip>
                import "CustomerX_Policy" "LocalPref_100"
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip>` with the specific neighbor IP address where this policy should be applied.
