## User question:
"How to configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 paths per unlabeled IPv6 unicast prefix while disabling the receive capability?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 paths per unlabeled IPv6 unicast prefix while disabling the receive capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv6
        multipath 8 ipv6
    exit
    no rapid-update ipv6
exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable equal treatment of eBGP and iBGP paths for IPv6 (`ebgp-ibgp-equal ipv6`)
2. Set the maximum number of multipaths to 8 for IPv6 (`multipath 8 ipv6`)
3. Disable rapid updates for IPv6, effectively limiting receive capabilities (`no rapid-update ipv6`)

Note that the actual path advertisement count will depend on your network topology and available paths, but this configuration allows up to 8 paths to be advertised per IPv6 prefix.
