To configure the Nokia router to declare a TCP connection down after missing 15 consecutive keepalives, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    keepalive 60
exit
```

This sets the BGP keepalive timer to 60 seconds. The default hold time is typically 3 times the keepalive interval (180 seconds), meaning missing 3 keepalives would declare the neighbor down. 

However, the reference content does not provide direct control over the number of missed keepalives before declaring a connection down. The closest available configuration is adjusting the keepalive interval itself. To achieve approximately 15 missed keepalives, you would need to set a very large keepalive interval, but this is not recommended as it would significantly delay failure detection.

For TCP-level keepalives (not BGP), you could configure:
```
configure bmp station "station_name" connection tcp-keepalive
    keep-interval 900
exit
```

This sets the TCP keepalive probe interval to 900 seconds (15 minutes). After 15 missed probes (approximately 225 minutes), the connection would be declared down.
