commit
匹配的cli
summary automatic
undo summary automatic
查询的def
The summary automatic command enables automatic aggregation for the locally-imported routes.
The undo summary automatic command disables automatic aggregation for the locally-imported routes.
By default, the locally-imported routes are not aggregated automatically.
检索到的def
This command sets the router ID in the BGP aggregator path attribute to zero when BGP aggregates routes. This prevents different routers within an AS from creating aggregate routes that contain different AS paths.
检索到的def
This command enables or disables Accumulated IGP (AIGP) path attribute support with one or more BGP peers. BGP path selection among routes with an associated AIGP metric is based on the end-to-end IGP metrics of the different BGP paths, even when these BGP paths span more than one AS and IGP instance.
匹配的cli
summary automatic
undo summary automatic
查询的def
The summary automatic command enables automatic aggregation for the locally-imported routes.
The undo summary automatic command disables automatic aggregation for the locally-imported routes.
By default, the locally-imported routes are not aggregated automatically.
检索到的def
This command sets the router ID in the BGP aggregator path attribute to zero when BGP aggregates routes. This prevents different routers within an AS from creating aggregate routes that contain different AS paths.
检索到的def
This command enables or disables Accumulated IGP (AIGP) path attribute support with one or more BGP peers. BGP path selection among routes with an associated AIGP metric is based on the end-to-end IGP metrics of the different BGP paths, even when these BGP paths span more than one AS and IGP instance.
input_text
You are an expert assistant in configuring network devices. Based on the user's request and the retrieved content from the router configuration manual below, generate appropriate CLI configuration commands.

---

User Request:  
How to configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 labeled-unicast IPv4 paths per prefix and negotiate to receive multiple paths?

Retrieved Reference Content (from the configuration manual):  
{
    "PageTitle": "aigp",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables or disables Accumulated IGP (AIGP) path attribute support with one or more BGP peers. BGP path selection among routes with an associated AIGP metric is based on the end-to-end IGP metrics of the different BGP paths, even when these BGP paths span more than one AS and IGP instance.",
    "CLIs": [
        "aigp",
        "no aigp"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no aigp"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "primary-ip-address",
    "FuncDef": "This command specifies the primary IP address of a reference location used for BGP optimal route reflection. Up to three IPv4 addresses and three IPv6 addresses can be specified per location.",
    "CLIs": [
        "primary-ip-address <ipv4-address>",
        "no primary-ip-address"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>orr>location"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "ipv4-address",
            "Info": "Specifies the primary IPv4 address of a location expressed in dotted decimal notation. Values-a.b.c.d."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no primary-ip-address"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "import",
    "FuncDef": "This command specifies route policies that control the handling of inbound routes received from certain peers. Route policies are configured in theconfig>router>policy-optionscontext.",
    "CLIs": [
        "import <plcy-or-long-expr> [ <plcy-or-expr> [ <plcy-or-expr> ] ]",
        "no import"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "plcy-or-long-expr",
            "Info": "Specifies the route policy name (up to 64 characters long) or a policy logical expression (up to 255 characters long). Allowed values are any string up to 255 characters long composed of printable, 7-bit ASCII characters. If the string contains special characters (#, $, spaces, and so on), the entire string must be enclosed within double quotes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "plcy-or-expr",
            "Info": "Specifies the route policy name (up to 64 characters long) or a policy logical expression (up to 64 characters long). Allowed values are any string up to 64 characters long composed of printable, 7-bit ASCII characters. If the string contains special characters (#, $, spaces, and so on), the entire string must be enclosed within double quotes."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no import"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors",
    "FuncDef": "This command allows BGP routes marked as LLGR stale to be advertised to BGP peers that did not advertise the LLGR capability when the session was opened. Thenoversion of this command causes advertisement behavior to follow the rule that stale routes cannot be advertised to a peer that does not understand or implement the LLGR capability. Stale routes are withdrawn towards such peers.",
    "CLIs": [
        "advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors [ without-no-export | no without-no-export ]",
        "no advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>graceful-restart>long-lived",
        "config>router>bgp>group>graceful-restart>long-lived",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>graceful-restart>long-lived"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "without-no-export",
            "Info": "Allows LLGR stale routes to be advertised to all peers, such that they can exit the local AS."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no advertise-stale-to-all-neighbors"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "next-hop-self",
    "FuncDef": "This command configures BGP to advertise routes to members of a group or to a specific neighbor using a local address of the BGP instance as the BGP next-hop address. Note thatnext-hop-selfis set without exception, regardless of the route source (EBGP or IBGP) or its family. When used with VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6 routes theenable-rr-vpn-forwardingcommand should also be configured.",
    "CLIs": [
        "next-hop-self",
        "no next-hop-self"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no next-hop-self"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "leak-import",
    "FuncDef": "This command is used to specify route policies that control the importation of leak-eligible routes from the BGP RIB of another routing instance into the unlabeled-IPv4, unlabeled-IPv6, or labeled-IPv4 RIB of the base router. To leak a route from one routing instance to another, the origin and destination RIB types must be the same; for example, it is not possible to leak a route from an unlabeled-IPv4 RIB of a VPRN into the labeled-IPv4 RIB of the base router.",
    "CLIs": [
        "leak-import <plcy-or-long-expr> [ <plcy-or-expr> ]",
        "no leak-import"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>rib-management>ipv4",
        "config>router>bgp>rib-management>label-ipv4",
        "config>router>bgp>rib-management>ipv6"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "plcy-or-long-expr",
            "Info": "Specifies up to 14 route policy names (up to 64 characters long) or a policy logical expression (up to 255 characters long). Allowed values are any string up to 255 characters long composed of printable, 7-bit ASCII characters. If the string contains special characters (#, $, spaces, and so on), the entire string must be enclosed within double quotes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "plcy-or-expr",
            "Info": "The route policy name (up to 64 characters long) or a policy logical expression (up to 64 characters long). Allowed values are any string up to 64 characters long composed of printable, 7-bit ASCII characters. If the string contains special characters (#, $, spaces, and so on), the entire string must be enclosed within double quotes."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no leak-import"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "enable-peer-tracking",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables BGP peer tracking. BGP peer tracking allows a BGP peer to be dropped immediately if the route used to resolve the BGP peer address is removed from the IP routing table and there is no alternative available. The BGP peer will not wait for the holdtimer to expire; therefore, the BGP re-convergence process is accelerated.",
    "CLIs": [
        "enable-peer-tracking",
        "no enable-peer-tracking"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no enable-peer-tracking"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "ebgp-ibgp-equal",
    "FuncDef": "This command instructs the BGP decision process to ignore the difference between EBGP and IBGP routes in selecting the best path and eligible multipaths (if multipath and ECMP are enabled). The result is a form of EIBGP load-balancing in a multipath scenario.",
    "CLIs": [
        "ebgp-ibgp-equal [ ipv4 ] [ ipv6 ] [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ] [ vpn-ipv4 ] [ vpn-ipv6 ]",
        "no ebgp-ibgp-equal"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>best-path-selection"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "ipv4",
            "Info": "Specifies that the command should be applied to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "ipv6",
            "Info": "Specifies that the command should be applied to unlabeled unicast IPv6 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "label-ipv4",
            "Info": "Specifies that the command should be applied to labeled unicast IPv4 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "label-ipv6",
            "Info": "Specifies that the command should be applied to labeled unicast IPv6 routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "vpn-ipv4",
            "Info": "Specifies that the command should be applied to IPv4 VPN routes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "vpn-ipv6",
            "Info": "Specifies that the command should be applied to IPv6 VPN routes."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no ebgp-ibgp-equal"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "ibgp-multipath",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables IBGP multipath load balancing when adding BGP routes to the route table if the route resolving the BGP nexthop offers multiple nexthops.",
    "CLIs": [
        "ibgp-multipath",
        "no ibgp-multipath"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no ibgp-multipath"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "primary-ipv6-address",
    "FuncDef": "This command specifies the primary IPv6 address of a reference location used for BGP optimal route reflection. Up to three IPv4 addresses and three IPv6 addresses can be specified per location.",
    "CLIs": [
        "primary-ipv6-address <ipv6-address>",
        "no primary-ipv6-address"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>orr>location"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "ipv6-address",
            "Info": "Specifies the primary IPv6 address of a location expressed in dotted decimal notation. Values-ipv6-address:."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no primary-ipv6-address"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "extended-nh-encoding",
    "FuncDef": "This command configures BGP to advertise (at session OPEN) the capability to receive label IPv4, VPN IPv4 routes, or IPv6 next hops from the peers. These peers should not send such routes unless they receive notification of this capability. If the SR OS router receives a label IPv4 or VPN IPv4 route from a peer to which it did not advertise the necessary capability, the UPDATE message will be considered malformed and this will cause either session reset ortreat-as-withdrawbehavior depending on the error handling settings.",
    "CLIs": [
        "extended-nh-encoding [ label-ipv4 ] [ vpn-ipv4 ]",
        "no extended-nh-encoding"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "label-ipv4",
            "Info": "Instructs BGP to advertise an extended NH encoding capability for NLRI AFI=1, NLRI SAFI=4, and next-hop AFI=2."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "vpn-ipv4",
            "Info": "Instructs BGP to advertise an extended NH encoding capability for NLRI AFI=1, NLRI SAFI=128, and next-hop AFI=2."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no extended-nh-encoding"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "export",
    "FuncDef": "This command specifies route policies that control the handling of outbound routes transmitted to certain peers. Route policies are configured in theconfig>router>policy-optionscontext.",
    "CLIs": [
        "export <plcy-or-long-expr> [ <plcy-or-expr> [ <plcy-or-expr> ] ]",
        "no export [ <plcy-or-long-expr> ]"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "plcy-or-long-expr",
            "Info": "Specifies the route policy name (up to 64 characters) or a policy logical expression (up to 255 characters long). Allowed values are any string up to 255 characters long composed of printable, 7-bit ASCII characters. If the string contains special characters (#, $, spaces, and so on), the entire string must be enclosed within double quotes."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "plcy-or-expr",
            "Info": "Specifies up to 14 route policy names (up to 64 characters each) or a policy logical expression (up to 64 characters long). Allowed values are any string up to 64 characters long composed of printable, 7-bit ASCII characters. If the string contains special characters (#, $, spaces, and so on), the entire string must be enclosed within double quotes."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no export"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "route-target-list",
    "FuncDef": "This command specifies the route target(s) to be accepted from or advertised to peers. If theroute-target-listis a non-null list, only routes with one or more of the given route targets are accepted from or advertised to peers.",
    "CLIs": [
        "route-target-list <comm-id> [ <comm-id> ]",
        "no route-target-list [ <comm-id> ]"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "comm-id",
            "Info": "Specifies up to 15 route target communities. Values-[target: {ip-address:comm-val | 2byte-asnumber:ext-comm-val | 4byte-asnumber:comm-val}."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no route-target-list"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "enable-rr-vpn-forwarding",
    "FuncDef": "When this command is configured all received VPN-IP routes, regardless of route target, are imported into the dummy VRF, where the BGP next-hops are resolved. Thelabel-route-transport-tunnelunderconfig>router>bgp>next-hop-resolutiondetermines what types of tunnels are eligible to resolve the next-hops. If a received VPN-IP route from IBGP peer X is resolved and selected as best so that it can be re-advertised to an IBGP peer Y, and the BGP next-hop is modified towards peer Y (by using the next-hop-self command in Y s group or neighbor context or by using a next-hop action in an export policy applied to Y) then BGP allocates a new VPRN service label value for the route, signals that new label value to Y and programs the IOM to do the corresponding label swap operation. The supported combinations of X and Y are outlined below:",
    "CLIs": [
        "enable-rr-vpn-forwarding",
        "no enable-rr-vpn-forwarding"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no enable-rr-vpn-forwarding"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "rapid-withdrawal",
    "FuncDef": "This command disables the delay (Minimum Route Advertisement) on sending BGP withdrawals. Normal route withdrawals may be delayed up to the minimum route advertisement to allow for efficient packing of BGP updates.",
    "CLIs": [
        "rapid-withdrawal",
        "no rapid-withdrawal"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no rapid-withdrawal"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "damp-peer-oscillations",
    "FuncDef": "This command controls how long a BGP peer session remains in the idle-state after some type of error causes the session to reset. In the idle state, BGP does not initiate or respond to attempts to establish a new session. Repeated errors that occur a short while after each session reset cause longer and longer hold times in the idle state. This command supports the DampPeerOscillations FSM behavior described in section 8.1 of RFC 4271,A Border Gateway Protocol 4 (BGP-4).",
    "CLIs": [
        "damp-peer-oscillations [ idle-hold-time <initial-wait> <second-wait> <max-wait> ] [ error-interval <minutes> ]"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "initial-wait",
            "Info": "The amount of time, in minutes, that a session remains in the idle-state after it has been stable for a while. Values-0 to 2048. ParamDefault: Default- 0"
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "second-wait",
            "Info": "A period of time, in minutes, that is doubled after each repeated session failure that occurs within a relatively short span of time. Values-1 to 2048. ParamDefault: Default- 5"
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "max-wait",
            "Info": "The maximum amount of time, in minutes, that a session remains in the idle-state after it has experienced repeated instability. Values-1 to 2048. ParamDefault: Default- 60"
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "minutes",
            "Info": "The interval of time, in minutes after a session reset, during which the session must be error-free in order to reset the penalty counter and return to idle-hold-time to initial-wait. Values-0 to 2048. ParamDefault: Default- 30"
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no damp-peer-oscillations"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "disable-capability-negotiation",
    "FuncDef": "This command disables capability negotiation. When the command is enabled and after the peering is flapped, any new capabilities are not negotiated and will strictly support IPv4 routing exchanges with that peer.",
    "CLIs": [
        "disable-capability-negotiation",
        "no disable-capability-negotiation"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no disable-capability-negotiation"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "label-ipv4",
    "FuncDef": "This command configures the add-paths capability for labeled-unicast IPv4 routes. By default, add-paths is not enabled for labeled-unicast IPv4 routes.",
    "CLIs": [
        "label-ipv4 send <send-limit>",
        "label-ipv4 send <send-limit> receive [ none ]",
        "no label-ipv4"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>add-paths",
        "config>router>bgp>group>add-paths",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor>add-paths"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "send-limit",
            "Info": "Specifies the maximum number of paths per labeled-unicast IPv4 prefix that are allowed to be advertised to add-paths peers. (The actual number of advertised routes may be less.) If the value is none, the router does not negotiate the send capability with respect to label-IPv4 AFI/SAFI. Values-1 to 16, none."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "receive",
            "Info": "Specifies the router negotiates to receive multiple labeled-unicast routes per IPv4 prefix."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "none",
            "Info": "Specifies that the router does not negotiate to receive multiple labeled-unicast routes per IPv4 prefix."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no label-ipv4"
}
{
    "PageTitle": "bgp",
    "FuncDef": "This command creates the BGP protocol instance and BGP configuration context. BGP is administratively enabled upon creation.",
    "CLIs": [
        "bgp",
        "no bgp"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": ""
}
{
    "PageTitle": "transport-tunnel",
    "FuncDef": "This command enables the context to configure options for the next-hop resolution of BGP labeled routes (VPN-IP and labeled-unicast) using tunnels in TTM. The context allows the selection of different tunnel resolution options for different types of BGP labeled routes: label-unicast IPv4, label-unicast IPv6, and VPN-IP routes (both VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6).",
    "CLIs": [
        "transport-tunnel"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>next-hop-res>labeled-routes"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": ""
}
{
    "PageTitle": "prefix-limit",
    "FuncDef": "This command configures the maximum number of BGP routes that can be received from a peer before some administrative action is taken. The administrative action can be the generation of a log event or taking down the session. If a session is taken down, then it can be brought back up automatically after an idle-timeout period, or else it can be configured to stay down ('forever') until the operator performs a reset.",
    "CLIs": [
        "prefix-limit <family> <limit> [ threshold <percentage> ] [ idle-timeout { <minutes> | forever } | log-only ] [ post-import ]",
        "no prefix-limit <family>"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "log-only",
            "Info": "Enables the warning message to be sent at the specified threshold percentage, and also when the limit is reached. However, the BGP session is not taken down."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "percentage",
            "Info": "Specifies the threshold value (as a percentage) that triggers a warning message to be sent. Values-1 to 100."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "family",
            "Info": "Specifies the address family to which the limit applies. Values-ipv4, label-ipv4, vpn-ipv4, ipv6, label-ipv6, vpn-ipv6, mcast-ipv4, l2-vpn, mvpn-ipv4, mdt-safi, ms-pw, flow-ipv4, route-target, mcast-vpn-ipv4, mvpn-ipv6, flow-ipv6, evpn, mcast-ipv6, bgp-ls."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "limit",
            "Info": "Specifies the number of routes that can be learned from a peer expressed as a decimal integer. Values-1 to 4294967295."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "minutes",
            "Info": "Specifies duration in minutes before automatically re-establishing a session. Values-1 to 1024."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "forever",
            "Info": "Specifies that the session is reestablished only after clear router bgp command is executed."
        },
        {
            "Parameters": "post-import",
            "Info": "Specifies that the limit should be applied only to the number of routes that are accepted by import policies."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": ""
}
{
    "PageTitle": "enforce-first-as",
    "FuncDef": "When this command is configured so that it applies to an EBGP session, all routes (belonging to all address families) that are received from the EBGP peer are checked to ensure that the most recent autonomous system number (ASN) in the AS_PATH attribute of each route matches the configuredpeer-asof the session; if it does not match, then either the session is reset (ifupdate-fault-toleranceis not enabled) or the session is left up but the route is treated as withdrawn (ifupdate-fault-toleranceis enabled).",
    "CLIs": [
        "enforce-first-as"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": ""
}
{
    "PageTitle": "aggregator-id-zero",
    "FuncDef": "This command sets the router ID in the BGP aggregator path attribute to zero when BGP aggregates routes. This prevents different routers within an AS from creating aggregate routes that contain different AS paths.",
    "CLIs": [
        "aggregator-id-zero",
        "no aggregator-id-zero"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "config>router>bgp",
        "config>router>bgp>group",
        "config>router>bgp>group>neighbor"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": null,
    "ExtraInfo": "Default: no aggregator-id-zero"
