To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 labeled-unicast IPv6 paths per prefix and disable receiving multiple paths from BGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp best-path-selection
    ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6
    multipath 8 label-ipv6
exit
```

To disable receiving multiple paths from BGP peers, apply a strict import policy that filters unwanted paths:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-IP>
    import "strict-policy"
exit
```

Note: You'll need to create a corresponding "strict-policy" under `config>router>policy-options` that limits accepted routes as needed for your specific requirements.
