To configure labeled BGP routes' next-hop resolution on a Nokia router, you'll need to work in the BGP configuration context. Here are the relevant CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        best-path-selection
            ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv4 label-ipv6
        exit
        group <group-name>
            next-hop-self
        exit
```

The `ebgp-ibgp-equal` command under `best-path-selection` with `label-ipv4` and/or `label-ipv6` parameters enables equal treatment of EBGP and IBGP paths for labeled routes. The `next-hop-self` command ensures proper next-hop resolution by advertising routes with the local BGP instance's address as the next hop.
------------
