To enable LDP tunneling for next-hop resolution of /32 IPv4 FECs on a Nokia router, you need to configure BGP to use labeled IPv4 routes and enable next-hop resolution via BGP routes. Here are the required CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-res
        use-bgp-routes
    exit
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable BGP to use BGP routes for recursive next-hop resolution (`use-bgp-routes`)
2. Enable extended next-hop encoding capability for labeled IPv4 routes (`extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4`)

This configuration allows the router to use LDP tunneling for resolving /32 IPv4 FEC next-hops through labeled IPv4 BGP routes.
