To configure LDP tunneling for resolving next-hops of /32 IPv4 FECs and /128 IPv6 FECs on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    policy <policy-name>
exit
```

Replace `<policy-name>` with your specific route policy name that controls which IP routes in RTM are eligible to resolve the BGP next-hop addresses. This policy will apply to both IPv4 and IPv6 routes.

Note: You'll need to create the appropriate route policy separately in the `config>router>policy-options` context to define which routes should be eligible for next-hop resolution via LDP tunneling.
