To configure a Nokia router to attach a link-bandwidth extended community to BGP routes advertised to a specific EBGP neighbor, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip>
link-bandwidth
send-to-ebgp ipv4
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<neighbor-ip>` with the specific neighbor's IP address. This will enable the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv4 routes advertised to that EBGP neighbor.
