To configure a Nokia router to attach a link-bandwidth extended community to BGP routes advertised to a specific EBGP peer, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            link-bandwidth
                send-to-ebgp ipv4
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the specific peer's IP address. This will enable sending the link-bandwidth extended community for IPv4 routes to that EBGP peer. 

For other address families (like ipv6), include them as additional parameters in the `send-to-ebgp` command, separated by spaces.
