## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to use the interface named "core-link1" as the source IP address for BGP sessions within a specific group?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure the Nokia router to use the interface named "core-link1" as the source IP address for BGP sessions within a specific group, you need to first identify the IP address assigned to "core-link1". Then, apply that IP as the local-address for the BGP group. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group <group-name>
            local-address <ip-address-of-core-link1>
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address-of-core-link1>` with the actual IP address configured on the "core-link1" interface. 

Note: The `local-address` command was not explicitly shown in the provided reference content, but it is a standard BGP parameter in Nokia routers for specifying the source IP address. If this exact command syntax isn't available in your router version, you would need to consult additional documentation for the correct parameter name.
