Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure a BGP peer with virtual AS number 65535 while hiding both local and global AS numbers:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        local-as 65535 private no-prepend-global-as
        peer-as <remote-peer-as-number>
        neighbor <remote-peer-ip-address>
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>`, `<remote-peer-as-number>`, and `<remote-peer-ip-address>` with your specific values. This configuration:
1. Sets the virtual AS number to 65535
2. Hides the local AS in received paths (`private` parameter)
3. Prevents prepending the global AS in advertised paths (`no-prepend-global-as` parameter)
