Here are the CLI configuration commands to configure a BGP neighbor with virtual AS 65535 while hiding both local and global AS numbers:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        peer-as <peer-as-number>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip>
            local-as 65535 private no-prepend-global-as
```

Explanation:
- `local-as 65535` sets the virtual AS number to 65535
- `private` hides the local AS in paths learned from the peer
- `no-prepend-global-as` prevents prepending the global AS in paths advertised to the peer

Replace `<group-name>`, `<peer-as-number>`, and `<neighbor-ip>` with your specific values.
