To configure the BGP local-preference attribute with a value of 200 on a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp local-preference 200
```

This command sets the local-preference value to 200 at the global BGP level. You can also apply it at the group or neighbor level if needed:

For a specific BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> local-preference 200
```

For a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> local-preference 200
```
------------
