To configure a Nokia router to discard routes containing AS 65530 in the AS path while maintaining the BGP session, you need to create an import policy that rejects routes with the specified AS in their path. Here are the CLI commands:

```
# Configure a route policy to reject routes containing AS 65530
configure router policy-options
begin
policy-statement REJECT_AS65530
entry 10
from as-path ".*65530.*"   # Regular expression matching AS 65530 anywhere in the path
action reject
exit
commit
exit

# Apply the policy to the BGP neighbor/group
configure router bgp group <group-name>
neighbor <ip-address>
import REJECT_AS65530
exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the specific neighbor IP address where you want to apply this filtering. This configuration will silently discard routes containing AS 65530 while keeping the BGP session active.
