How should Nokia routers handle BGP routes when detecting the local AS number (e.g., AS65530) in the AS path while maintaining the peer session?
---
## Proposed answer:
To handle BGP routes when detecting the local AS number (AS65530) in the AS path while maintaining the peer session, configure the `loop-detect` parameter with the `ignore-loop` option:

```
configure router bgp
    loop-detect ignore-loop
exit
```

This configuration will ignore routes with loops in the AS path (including your local AS65530) but maintain the BGP peering session. 

If you want to apply this setting to specific groups or neighbors instead of globally, use these alternative configurations:

For a group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    loop-detect ignore-loop
exit
```

For a neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address>
    loop-detect ignore-loop
exit
```
