To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes with a MED value of 5000 when MED is not already specified, you need to create and apply a route policy that sets the MED value. Here’s how to do it:

1. **Create a route policy to set the MED value**:
   ```
   configure router policy-options
   begin
   policy-statement SET_MED
     entry 10
       action accept
         med set 5000
     exit
   commit
   ```

2. **Apply the policy to BGP export**:
   ```
   configure router bgp
   group <group-name>
     neighbor <neighbor-ip>
       export SET_MED
   exit
   commit
   ```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<neighbor-ip>` with your specific BGP group and neighbor details. This ensures that all advertised BGP routes will have a MED value of 5000 unless explicitly set otherwise.
