To configure a Nokia router to advertise BGP routes with a fixed MED value of 15000 when the MED is not explicitly set, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        always-compare-med infinity
exit
```

This configuration will treat routes without an explicit MED value as having an infinite MED (2^32-1), effectively making them less preferred. However, note that this doesn't directly set a fixed MED of 15000 - it only handles how routes without MED are treated during path selection.

The reference material does not provide a direct way to set a default MED value of 15000 for routes where MED isn't explicitly set. The closest available option is the `always-compare-med infinity` command which assigns the highest possible MED value to routes without an explicit MED.
