To configure Nokia routers to retain all MP-BGP routes in RIB-IN without requiring route refresh messages after VPN policy changes, you need to enable the `rapid-withdrawal` feature under the BGP configuration context. This ensures immediate processing of route withdrawals without waiting for route advertisements.

Here's the CLI command:

```
configure router bgp rapid-withdrawal
```

This command disables the delay on sending BGP withdrawals, allowing the router to immediately process route updates without waiting for route refresh messages when VPN policies change.
