## User question:
"How to configure Nokia routers to encode type/subtype in advertised BGP MVPN routes as 0x010b?"
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to encode type/subtype in advertised BGP MVPN routes as 0x010b, use the following CLI command:

```
configure router bgp rapid-update mvpn-ipv4
```

This command enables BGP rapid update for the MVPN IPv4 address family, which includes the type/subtype encoding in the advertised routes. The default encoding for MVPN routes follows the standard format where the type/subtype is represented as 0x010b when rapid update is enabled for mvpn-ipv4.
