Here are the CLI commands to configure a BGP peer with IP address 192.0.2.15 on a Nokia router:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor 192.0.2.15
            peer-as <remote-as-number>
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name and `<remote-as-number>` with the autonomous system number of the remote peer. 

Additional optional parameters you may want to configure include:
- `router-id <ip-address>`
- `connect-retry <seconds>`
- `next-hop-self`
- `enable-peer-tracking`
- `third-party-nexthop`

These would be added under the appropriate hierarchy levels (global BGP, group, or neighbor configuration).
