To configure a Nokia router's BGP group to always use its own interface IP as the next-hop for advertised routes, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        next-hop-self
exit all
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the name of your BGP group. This ensures the router advertises routes to members of the specified group using its local BGP instance address as the next-hop.
