To configure a Nokia router's BGP group to always use its local interface IP as the next-hop address when advertising routes, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        next-hop-self
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your actual BGP group name. This will ensure the router uses its local interface IP as the next-hop address for all routes advertised to peers in this group.
