---
## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to preserve BGP next-hop information for both IPv4 and IPv6 routes when advertising to peers within the same group?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to preserve BGP next-hop information for both IPv4 and IPv6 routes when advertising to peers within the same group, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        no next-hop-self
        third-party-nexthop
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the actual name of your BGP peer group. 

These commands:
1. Disable `next-hop-self` for the group (which would otherwise override the original next-hop)
2. Enable `third-party-nexthop` to preserve the original next-hop information when advertising routes to peers in the same subnet

This configuration ensures that both IPv4 and IPv6 routes maintain their original next-hop information when advertised to peers within the same group.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
next-hop-unchanged [ label-ipv4 ] [ label-ipv6 ]
no next-hop-unchanged
FuncDef:
This command enables unchanged BGP next-hops when sending BGP routes to peers in this group.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
