To configure a Nokia router to enable unchanged BGP next-hops for both IPv4 and IPv6 labeled routes when advertising to peers in a specific group, you need to disable the `next-hop-self` feature for that group. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        no next-hop-self
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with the actual name of your BGP peer group. This configuration ensures that BGP will preserve the original next-hop addresses when advertising labeled IPv4 and IPv6 routes to peers in the specified group.
