## User question:
Configure Nokia routers to enable BGP optimization for reducing redundant route advertisements between route reflectors.
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure BGP optimization for reducing redundant route advertisements between route reflectors on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    cluster <cluster-id> orr-location <location-id>
    location <location-id> primary-ip-address <ipv4-address>
exit
```

Replace `<cluster-id>` with your route reflector cluster ID (e.g., 192.0.2.1), `<location-id>` with a value between 1-16, and `<ipv4-address>` with the primary IP address for the location.

For additional optimization, you may want to enable AIGP path attribute support:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    aigp
exit
``` 

And configure next-hop-self for route reflector groups:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name>
    next-hop-self
exit
```
