To disable BGP session initiation attempts while maintaining existing connections in a Nokia router, use the following CLI command:

```
config>router>bgp damp-peer-oscillations idle-hold-time 0 0 0
```

This command sets the idle hold time to zero at all levels (`initial-wait`, `second-wait`, and `max-wait`), effectively preventing new session initiation attempts while keeping established sessions active.
