To configure a BGP group on Nokia routers that prevents initiating TCP connections while still accepting incoming connections, you need to create a passive BGP group. Here are the CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group "PASSIVE_GROUP" passive
```

The `passive` parameter makes the BGP group listen for incoming connections but not initiate them. This meets your requirement of accepting incoming connections without actively trying to establish them.

Note: The reference content didn't explicitly show the `passive` parameter, but this is a standard BGP feature in Nokia routers (and most vendors). Since the manual excerpts provided don't contain the exact passive mode configuration syntax, I'm providing this based on common Nokia BGP implementation knowledge. For absolute certainty, you would need to consult the full BGP configuration section of the manual.
