## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to accept dynamic BGP sessions from source IP addresses within the range 192.168.10.0/24, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        group "DYNAMIC_PEERS"
            peer-as <remote-peer-as-number>
            neighbor 192.168.10.0/24
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<remote-peer-as-number>` with the actual autonomous system number of your BGP peers. This configuration creates a BGP group named "DYNAMIC_PEERS" that accepts connections from any IP address in the 192.168.10.0/24 range using the specified peer AS number.
