To configure a Nokia router to accept dynamic BGP sessions from peers within the 192.168.100.0/24 subnet, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        peer-as <remote-peer-as-number>
        neighbor 192.168.100.0/24
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `<remote-peer-as-number>` with the actual autonomous system number of your BGP peers. This configuration creates a BGP group named "DYNAMIC_PEERS" that accepts connections from any peer in the 192.168.100.0/24 subnet. 

Additional optional parameters you may want to configure include:
```
configure router bgp
    router-id <your-router-id>
    group DYNAMIC_PEERS
        connect-retry <seconds>
        next-hop-self
        third-party-nexthop
        exit
    exit
```
