To configure a Nokia router to strip private AS numbers from BGP updates while preserving AS64500 and matching peer AS numbers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            remove-private limited skip-peer-as
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP group name and `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's IP address. The `limited` parameter ensures private ASNs are only stripped up to the first public ASN (preserving AS64500), while `skip-peer-as` preserves any private ASN that matches the peer's AS number.
