To configure BGP next-hop resolution for labeled routes in Nokia routers when transport tunnels require a specific address family, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            rr-use-route-table
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables the router to use the route table for resolving BGP next-hops of labeled IPv4 and IPv6 routes, which is particularly useful when the router (such as a Route Reflector) does not participate in tunnel signaling protocols like LDP or RSVP.
