Please generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Do not invent commands or parameters that are not present in the provided reference.
Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure a Nokia router to bind BGP labeled routes only to specific tunnel types under the resolution-filter, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family
                    resolution-filter
                        [no] sr-isis
                        [no] sr-ospf3
                        [no] sr-te
```

Replace `[no]` with the desired tunnel types you want to include (remove `[no]` to enable or add `no` to disable). For example, to enable only SR-ISIS and SR-TE tunnels:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family
                    resolution-filter
                        sr-isis
                        no sr-ospf3
                        sr-te
``` 

This configuration will restrict BGP labeled route binding to only the selected tunnel types in the resolution filter.
