## User question:
How to configure a Nokia router to enable BGP prefix resolution using only LDP and RSVP-TE tunnels while excluding other tunnel types?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to enable BGP prefix resolution using only LDP and RSVP-TE tunnels while excluding other tunnel types, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv4
                    resolution-filter
                        rsvp-te
                        ldp
                        no bgp
```

This configuration ensures that BGP prefix resolution for labeled routes will only use RSVP-TE and LDP tunnels, explicitly excluding BGP tunnels. The `no bgp` command removes BGP from the resolution filter.
