## Proposed answer:
To configure a Nokia router to bind BGP prefixes exclusively to tunnel types specified in the resolution-filter for BGP shortcut next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-res labeled-routes transport-tunnel
```

This command enters the context where you can specify the tunnel types for BGP labeled routes (VPN-IP and labeled-unicast) in the next-hop resolution process. From here, you can apply specific filters or policies to restrict the tunnel types used for BGP shortcut next-hop resolution. 

