To configure a Nokia router to enable BGP Monitoring Protocol (BMP) for sending only post-policy route monitoring messages, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure
    bmp
        station <station-name>
            no report-local-routes
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enters the BMP configuration context
2. Creates a BMP station
3. Disables local route reporting (which ensures only post-policy routes are sent)
4. Exits back to the root configuration level

Note that you'll need to replace `<station-name>` with your actual BMP station name and may need additional configuration for the BMP station connection parameters depending on your specific setup.
