To configure Nokia routers to use RSVP tunnels with the best metric for BGP next-hop resolution when resolving IPv4 destinations, use the following CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        shortcut-tunnels
            family ipv4
                resolution-filter
                    rsvp
                    sr-ospf
                exit
            exit
        exit
        policy <policy-name>
    exit
exit
```

Key points:
- Enable RSVP tunnels in the resolution filter for IPv4 family
- Include `sr-ospf` if Segment Routing OSPF tunnels should also be considered
- Optionally apply a policy to control which routes are eligible for next-hop resolution

This configuration ensures BGP will prefer RSVP tunnels with the best metric when resolving next-hops for IPv4 destinations.
