To configure `2001:db8:cafe::2` as an additional IPv6 address for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    optimal-route-reflection
        location <location-id>
            primary-ipv6-address 2001:db8:cafe::2
```

Replace `<location-id>` with your specific location identifier (a value between 1 and 16). 

If you need to associate this location with a BGP cluster, you would additionally configure:
```
configure router bgp
    cluster <cluster-id> orr-location <location-id>
```

Again replacing `<cluster-id>` and `<location-id>` with appropriate values.
