Please generate CLI configuration commands that fulfill the user's request using the information from the reference content. Do not invent commands or parameters that are not present in the provided reference.
Please respond directly to the user's question. Do not mention phrases like "based on the information you provided", "according to the documentation", or anything similar.
To configure Nokia routers to advertise the link-bandwidth extended community for unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes to EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

If you need to apply this to a specific EBGP neighbor instead of the whole group:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            link-bandwidth
                send-to-ebgp ipv4
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

These commands enable the advertising of link-bandwidth extended communities for unlabeled IPv4 routes to EBGP peers.
