How to configure Nokia routers to add link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes when advertising to EBGP peers?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to add link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled unicast IPv4 routes when advertising to EBGP peers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your specific BGP group name. This configuration enables the sending of link-bandwidth extended community for IPv4 routes to EBGP peers within the specified group.
