To administratively disable BGP neighbor functionality on a Nokia router without removing its configuration, use the following CLI commands:

1. To disable a specific BGP neighbor:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <neighbor-ip> shutdown
```

2. To disable an entire BGP group:
```
configure router bgp group <group-name> shutdown
```

3. To disable the entire BGP instance while preserving the configuration:
```
configure router bgp shutdown
```

These commands will gracefully disable BGP functionality at different levels while maintaining all configuration settings.
------------
