## Proposed answer:
To prevent BGP routes from being reflected back to the originating peer on a Nokia router, you need to configure a route policy that filters out routes based on their origin. Here's the CLI configuration:

```
configure router
    policy-options
        begin
        policy-statement "prevent-reflection"
            entry 10
                from protocol bgp
                action reject
            exit
        commit
    exit
    bgp
        group "your-group-name"
            neighbor "peer-ip-address"
                export "prevent-reflection"
            exit
        exit
    exit
```

Replace `"your-group-name"` with your BGP group name and `"peer-ip-address"` with the IP address of the originating peer. This policy will block BGP routes from being advertised back to the originating peer.
