---
## User question:
How to configure Nokia routers to allow BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference IS-IS instance for next-hop resolution?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to allow BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference IS-IS instance for next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    extended-nh-encoding label-ipv4
exit
```

This command enables BGP to advertise the capability to receive labeled IPv4 routes, allowing Segment Routing tunnels to be used for next-hop resolution. Ensure your IS-IS instances are properly configured with appropriate preferences to influence the path selection.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
sr-isis
no sr-isis
FuncDef:
This command selects the Segment Routing (SR) tunnel type programmed by an IS-IS instance in TTM for next-hop resolution of BGP routes and labeled routes. This option allows BGP to use the segment- routing tunnel in the tunnel table submitted by the lowest preference IS-IS instance or, in case of a tie, the lowest numbered IS-IS instance.
