To enable segment routing tunnels from OSPFv3 instances for BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router, you'll need to configure the following:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        use-bgp-routes
        policy <policy-name>
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<policy-name>` with your specific route policy name that controls which IP routes are eligible for BGP next-hop resolution. This configuration allows BGP to use OSPFv3-learned segment routing tunnels for next-hop resolution.

Note that the reference material doesn't contain direct OSPFv3 segment routing configuration commands, but the above BGP next-hop resolution configuration will work with OSPFv3 segment routing tunnels when properly set up in the OSPFv3 configuration (which wasn't included in the provided reference content).
