## Proposed answer:
To configure Nokia routers to allow BGP to use Segment Routing tunnels from the lowest preference OSPF instance for next-hop resolution, use the following CLI commands:

```cli
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        policy "OSPF_LOWEST_PREFERENCE_POLICY"
    exit
exit
```

Where `"OSPF_LOWEST_PREFERENCE_POLICY"` is a route policy you need to create separately that matches routes from the lowest preference OSPF instance. The policy would look something like this:

```cli
configure router policy-options
    begin
    policy-statement "OSPF_LOWEST_PREFERENCE_POLICY"
        entry 10
            from protocol ospf
            from preference <lowest_ospf_preference_value>
            accept
        exit
    commit
exit
```

Replace `<lowest_ospf_preference_value>` with the actual preference value of your lowest priority OSPF instance. This ensures BGP will only use OSPF routes with this specific preference for next-hop resolution via Segment Routing tunnels.
