## User question:
How to enable Segment Routing TE tunnel selection for BGP next-hop resolution on a Nokia router when multiple tunnels have the same lowest metric?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable Segment Routing TE tunnel selection for BGP next-hop resolution when multiple tunnels have the same lowest metric, configure the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp next-hop-resolution
    use-bgp-routes
exit
```

This ensures that BGP routes are used for recursive next-hop resolution, allowing the selection among multiple tunnels with equal metrics.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
sr-te
no sr-te
FuncDef:
This command selects the Segment Routing (SR) tunnel type programmed by a traffic engineered (TE) instance in TTM for next-hop resolution. In the case of multiple SR-TE tunnels with the same lowest metric, BGP selects the tunnel with the lowest tunnel ID.
