To enable TCP connection keepalive monitoring on a Nokia router's BMP station, use the following CLI commands:

1. Navigate to the BMP station connection configuration:
```bash
configure
bmp
station <station-name>
connection
```

2. Configure the TCP keepalive interval (default is 15 seconds):
```bash
tcp-keepalive
keep-interval <desired_interval_in_seconds>
```

Replace `<station-name>` with your BMP station name and `<desired_interval_in_seconds>` with your preferred keepalive interval (1-100000). 

Example (setting interval to 20 seconds):
```bash
configure
bmp
station BMP_MONITOR
connection
tcp-keepalive
keep-interval 20
```
