To configure the third IPv6 address for BGP optimal route reflection on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp optimal-route-reflection
location <location-id> primary-ipv6-address 2001:db8:85a3::8a2e:370:7334
exit
```

Replace `<location-id>` with the appropriate location identifier (1 to 16). This will set the specified IPv6 address as the primary IPv6 address for the given location in the BGP optimal route reflection configuration.
