To configure a Nokia router to preserve the original BGP next-hop when advertising routes between EBGP peers within the same subnet, you need to disable the `next-hop-self` feature for the relevant BGP group or neighbor. Here's the CLI command:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> no next-hop-self
```

or for a specific neighbor:

```
configure router bgp group <group-name> neighbor <ip-address> no next-hop-self
```

Replace `<group-name>` and `<ip-address>` with your actual BGP group name and neighbor IP address. This ensures the original BGP next-hop is preserved when advertising routes to EBGP peers in the same subnet.
