How to configure Nokia routers to enable tunnel-based next-hop resolution for BGP labeled IPv6 unicast routes?
---
## Proposed answer:
To configure tunnel-based next-hop resolution for BGP labeled IPv6 unicast routes on Nokia routers, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            rr-use-route-table
        exit
    exit
exit
```

This configuration enables the router to use the route table for resolving next-hops of labeled IPv6 routes, which is particularly useful for route reflectors that don't participate in tunnel signaling protocols.
