To configure a BGP peer as external on a Nokia router, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        peer-as <remote-as-number>
exit
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your desired BGP group name and `<remote-as-number>` with the autonomous system number of the external peer. 

If you need to configure specific neighbors within this external group:
```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        type external
        peer-as <remote-as-number>
        neighbor <neighbor-ip-address>
    exit
exit
```

For basic external BGP peering, these commands establish the essential configuration. Additional parameters like `disable-capability-negotiation`, `next-hop-self`, or `enable-peer-tracking` can be added as needed under the group or neighbor contexts.
