To configure a Nokia router to advertise up to 8 diverse VPN-IPv4 paths to BGP peers while disabling the receive capability, use the following CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    add-paths
        vpn-ipv4 send 8 receive none
    exit
exit
```

This configuration:
1. Enables the add-paths capability under BGP
2. Specifically configures VPN-IPv4 routes to:
   - Send up to 8 paths per prefix (`send 8`)
   - Disable receiving multiple paths (`receive none`)

The configuration can be applied at the global BGP level, group level, or neighbor level depending on your specific requirements.
