## User question:
How to enable weighted load balancing for 6PE traffic over RSVP-TE tunnels on a Nokia router?
---
## Proposed answer:
To enable weighted load balancing for 6PE traffic over RSVP-TE tunnels on a Nokia router, you need to configure BGP to treat both eBGP and iBGP paths equally for labeled IPv6 routes and ensure proper next-hop resolution through RSVP-TE tunnels. Here are the required CLI commands:

```
configure router bgp
    best-path-selection
        ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6
    exit
    next-hop-resolution
        labeled-routes
            transport-tunnel
                family ipv6
                    resolution-filter
                        rsvp-te
                    exit
                exit
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

These commands:
1. Enable equal treatment of eBGP and iBGP paths for labeled IPv6 routes (`ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6`)
2. Configure next-hop resolution for IPv6 labeled routes to use RSVP-TE tunnels

This configuration allows BGP to consider both eBGP and iBGP paths as equal candidates for load balancing 6PE traffic across multiple RSVP-TE tunnels.
---
## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
weighted-ecmp
no weighted-ecmp
FuncDef:
This command enables weighted ECMP for next-hop tunnel selection for 6PE. When weighted ECMP is enabled, the RSVP-TE tunnel used to forward 6PE packets to the ECMP next hop is chosen according to the outcome of the hash on the packet at the normalized load-balancing weight of the tunnel.
ParaDef:
No ParaDef found
