To enable weighted load balancing for BGP next-hop tunnel selection in Nokia routers when using 6PE, configure the following commands:

```
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            policy <policy-name>
            use-bgp-routes
        exit
        best-path-selection
            ebgp-ibgp-equal label-ipv6
        exit
    exit
exit
```

Replace `<policy-name>` with your specific route policy name that controls which IP routes are eligible for BGP next-hop resolution. This configuration enables BGP to consider both eBGP and iBGP paths equally for labeled IPv6 routes (used in 6PE) and allows BGP routes to be used for recursive next-hop resolution.
